OL,3,ASummer 2026 was UK's hottest on record,
OL,4,AMet Office says
OL,5,
OL,6,FSummer 2026 was the UK's hottest on
OL,7,Frecord, according to provisional data
OL,8,Ffrom the Met Office.
OL,10,FFigures for the months of June, July
OL,11,Fand August show that the average mean
OL,12,Ftemperature - which includes day and
OL,13,Fovernight temperatures - was 16.5C, the
OL,14,Fwarmest on record in a dataset going
OL,15,Fback to 1884.
OL,17,FIt follows a spring and summer of
OL,18,Fpersistent heat with five widespread
OL,19,Fheatwaves and 40 days of temperatures
OL,20,Fabove 30C (86F), smashing the previous
OL,21,Frecord of 34 days.
OL,23,APub: 31-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG7/39
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
